 Amounts keep the precision they were written with and are added exactly.
 Reports display them rounded to two places, half to even.
 
+## Commodities
+
+An amount may be followed by a space and a commodity code of one to ten
+uppercase letters: `42.50 EUR`, `-3 AAPL`. An amount without a code is in the
+default commodity, which is displayed without a suffix. Each transaction must
+balance in every commodity separately. A posting may omit its amount only when
+all the other postings use the same commodity; it takes that commodity.
+
+## Prices
+
+A price directive starts in column one:
+
+```text
+P 2026-01-15 EUR 1.0850 USD
+```
+
+It records that on 2026-01-15 one EUR was worth 1.0850 USD. The rate must be
+a positive number; both codes follow the commodity rules above.
+
